-- examples/checks/agg-datastrat-retract-check.rofl — agg_datastrat_retract:
-- a base fact taken out of a world whose cells are stratified by their data
-- leaves the world a fresh evaluation without it would have, whatever the cells
-- it supported are: the delta path is not worked out for such a component and
-- the world is evaluated again. a4 is read by d1 and d2 and by what reads them
-- (e1, e2); each of those has a range with a cell that has no value, so none has
-- a total now, and every cell that never read a4 keeps its.
-- expect-row: value[main](c1,43) tick drv support=1
-- expect-row: value[main](b4,19) tick drv support=1
-- expect-row: value[main](f6,15) tick drv support=1
-- expect-no-row: value[main](d1,
-- expect-no-row: value[main](d2,
-- expect-no-row: value[main](e1,
-- expect-no-row: value[main](e2,
-- expect-no-row: value[main](a4,
